{"id":"neo-vectorheart","title":"Neo-Vectorheart","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Neo-Vectorheart","rev":239667,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neo-Vectorheart"]}," is an aesthetic that originated approximately in the late 2010s, as a pseudo-revival of the ",{"t":"a","c":["Vectorheart"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Vectorheart"}," aesthetic and part of the ",{"t":"a","c":["Neo-Y2K"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Neo-Y2K"}," movement. The aesthetic incorporates 45- and/or 60-degree angles; ",{"t":"a","c":["Neubrutalist"],"id":"neubrutalism"}," vernacular; bright, contrasting, and occasionally monochromatic color schemes; and maximalist motifs inspired by ",{"t":"a","c":["Cyberpunk"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cyberpunk"}," visuals and \"game]-grunge.\" The visual style found within Neo-Vectorheart prioritizes sleek, dynamic designs, often as an homage or pastiche of the work done by the design firms that popularized the original Vectorheart look."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["During the Late-2010s to the Early-2020s, there has been a resurgence in Vectorheart. This was inspired by similar Neo-Y2K movements going on at the same time. Neo-Vectorheart has come to be embraced by online gamers, it being said to incorporate maximalist \"gamer-grunge\". Neo-Vectorheart is also popular in the realm of logo design."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Neo-Vectorheart, similar to Vectorheart, is characterized by striking vector shapes, 45- and/or 60-degree diagonal lines, and futuristic fonts. It is distinguished from its predecessor due to its monochromatic color schemes and less abstract patterns than regular Vectorheart. Black and white are the most commonly found colors in this subgenre, with other colors generally being used as complimentary/accent colors rather than primary ones; this monochromatic motif also works well on logos, one of Neo-Vectorheart's primary categories."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Sports"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Formula 1 (2018 rebrand)"]},{"c":["Formula E (2026 rebrand)"]},{"c":["MotoGP (2025 rebrand)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Arknights: Endfield"]}," (2026)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Death Stranding"]}," series (2019-present)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Valorant"]}," (2020)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/20/Neo_vector1.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113301","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Methlab Records, Main Logo & Wordmark, Designed by dmas3 (c. 2015)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/96/Neo_vector2.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113322","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Audeka - Dark Energy / Direct Injection, Single - Design by Greenaway & Greenaway (2017)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/dd/Neo_vector3.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113341","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Designed by Ben Hook (N2-Antireal) (2019)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/3e/Neo_vector4.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113359","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Akira Complex - Hypersynthetic - Design by Ben Hook (N2-Antireal), Logo by Fredric Harbin (Serxphis) (2018)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/3c/Neo_vector5.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113412","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Riot Games, Valorant Logo & Wordmark, Designed by Cory Schmitz (2020)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0e/Neo_vector6.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113524","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["NeuroFunk Grid Logo"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c5/Neo_vector7.png/revision/latest?cb=20230824113537","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Neurohop Forum Logo & Wordmark"]},{"src":"https://static.